cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this method or code, please cite this repository."
title: "Virtual Hole Method: flushing holes in pump impeller blades modelled as cyclicACMI patch pairs with a handbook-based porous-baffle pressure jump (OpenFOAM)"
abstract: >-
  Holes drilled through centrifugal-pump impeller blades to flush gas accumulations
  are represented without changing CAD or mesh: blade faces inside each hole outline
  on the pressure and suction sides are coupled as a cyclicACMI pair, and the hole's
  hydraulic resistance (entrance, friction and Borda-Carnot exit losses after Idelchik)
  is imposed as a Darcy-Forchheimer pressure jump by the boundary condition
  porousBafflePressureAMI. Works for single-phase and Euler-Euler multiphase solvers
  in MRF impeller simulations (OpenFOAM Foundation v9).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Park
    given-names: Changkyu
    affiliation: "Chair of Hydraulic Fluid Machinery, Ruhr University Bochum"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cpark247/virtual-hole-method"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - OpenFOAM
  - centrifugal pump
  - impeller
  - gas accumulation
  - two-phase flow
  - boundary condition
  - cyclicACMI
  - porous baffle
  - hydraulic resistance
